<title>USA: US Mint buys 1,830 tonnes copper at avg $2.0608/kg.</title>
<headline>US Mint buys 1,830 tonnes copper at avg $2.0608/kg.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Mint said on Wednesday that it bought 1,830 tonnes of copper from four firms at an average price of $2.0608 per kg.</p>
<p>Awards went to:</p>
<p>-- Ore &amp; Chemical Corp, 1,196,000 kg for $2,467,946.00.</p>
<p>-- Gerald Metals, 538,000 kg for $1,104,083.60.</p>
<p>-- Minorco, 18,144 kg for $37,895.56.</p>
<p>-- Cerro Sales Corp, 77,856 kg for $161,297.15</p>
</text>
